{
 "notes": ["The three SV dealers on the town map (original scene 34, shared: create 0x3b19b, init 0x3af43, end 0x39d6a; menu 0x3a990, profile 0x3a5bc, trade 0x3a92a and 0x3a789, buy 0x3a618, hangars 0x3a2fe, notices 0x3abda, question 0x3ad84, leaving 0x3a500; draws 0x39e46, 0x396be, 0x399d8, 0x39585, 0x39db6). The town map sets which dealer (0x393de: American Stars 0, Kojima 1, Ventuno 2), which picks its look from the tables at 0x1fd708-0x1fddb8 (dealers.*) and its lineup from the day's calendar entry (tables/town.json dealers, by index): three SVs from tables/garage.json dealer_lineups, each a robot record and a name plate (pictures).", "opening: the band (1213) slides in from band_from over band_seconds (20 frames), then the menu's icons from slide_from, slide_distance along, over menu_seconds (40 frames, 0x19d440); welcome (1216) shows with the band and fades as the icons arrive ((1 - menu) x band, 0x39603). A press skips it. EXIT and NAME ENTRY run it backwards with farewell (1215) instead, then fade out. SV SPEC only fades to the selected robot; returning resumes the open menu at the same item, without a farewell or another welcome.", "panorama: the dealer's four backgrounds (640 x 480, the last 200 wide) side by side, scrolling left 0.5 a frame (scroll_speed) at half brightness (0x808080), wrapping. top, bottom and line (1212, stretched x100) frame it.", "menu: left/right over COMPANY PROFILE, the three SVs and EXIT (0x6d1cd flags 0x17, sys 3), the chosen icon lit over its plain one; an SV's icon is its legs' (0x1fd7a0 by legs record; legs_icons). Confirm (sys 5) opens the profile or the trade window; EXIT (sys 26) leaves; cancel moves to EXIT (sys 4). The help line says what confirm does (0x1fdd4c).", "logo: large at large_at (x 1.875) while the profile or EXIT is chosen, small at small_at over an SV, moving 0.125 a frame with a trail of 15 copies, each 0.7 of the opacity of the one before (0x393ee, 0x39e46); before the menu has opened it is drawn once at half opacity.", "SV chosen: the maker's badge at (40, 284), the SV's name plate at picture_at cross-fading from the last one over picture_seconds (0.05 a frame), and its price (0x392ff: the prices of its parts, modules, paint and emblem, times price_markup, the float 1.1 at 0x19b2a8, truncated, 0x39ca8) after the price label, right-aligned at 570 (0x39db6).", "profile: the panel grows open over 10 frames (0xbe87c), then the text script (0x1fdd88 by dealer, 0xc58ba) shows the corporation profile; the port closes it on confirm or cancel.", "trade: SV SPEC, BUY and CANCEL on the window (1194), the chosen label (0x1fd9c8) lit orange and pulsing; left/right (sys 4), cancel moves to CANCEL (sys 3). SV SPEC copies the SV to + 0x10f5c and opens its spec screen (spec_screen), which comes back here. BUY checks (0x3a618) each hangar: owned, empty, the SV has a body, legs and CHIP, and the stock has room for all of its parts and modules (0x39501). With one and the money: the hangars; otherwise no_stock (the stock is full), no_hangar or poor.", "hangars: left/right scroll the carousel of hangar numbers (0x1fddc4) 56 a step over 8 frames (sys 4), empty ones lit; confirm on one that does not fit says in_use or not_yours (not owned), otherwise pays, fits the SV (0x1da04, sys 27) and says delivered; cancel (sys 8) goes back to the trade window.", "after delivered: board asks YES/NO (NO first); YES rides it (+ 0x9c8) and says boarded. Then name_chip, and NAME ENTRY names the new CHIP (its stock entry; mode 2, 0x2c5d9) and comes back here (data/ui/name_entry.json exits).", "messages: the SYSTEM INFORMATION notices (0x1fdaa0, 0x4c each: lines, text at (139, 213))."],
